From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:02:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Share rebuilt interval metadata within one explicit cache
 owner

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the promoted
series (tree ea1281f880e7535e3d87725be0156a8e38fc2fb2), the independent
inactive-read guard and experimental cluster-search patches 0001/0003/0004.

Rationale: repeated queries of one cache need not decode the same keys
for each query. Rebuild one snapshot through the maximum visible extent,
then use that conservative superset for every row. Include extent reduction
and safe page-table expansion in candidate cost.

Quality: the API requires one explicitly owned page table, not mixed request
rows. Every call and graph replay rebuilds all metadata; no persistent cache
reuse or inferred ownership is introduced. Final scorer and tie order are
unchanged. Metadata reads only the union of the visible written key prefixes.

Tests: superset-bound and selected-position gates, changing visibility,
cache mutation and sanitizer tests are required. GPU qualification for this
optional grouped path remains pending.

Upstream status: local experimental candidate, not submitted upstream.
